  margin: 2.25rem 0 0.75rem;\n    letter-spacing: -0.01em;\n  }\n  .meta {\n    display: grid;\n    grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr;\n    gap: 0.5rem 1.5rem;\n    margin: 1.5rem 0;\n    font-size: 0.98rem;\n  }\n  .meta dt { color: var(--muted); }\n  .meta dd { margin: 0; font-weight: 500; }\n  ul { padding-left: 1.25rem; margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem; }\n  li { margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }\n  .cta {\n    display: inline-block;\n    background: var(--ink);\n    color: var(--paper);\n    text-decoration: none;\n    padding: 0.85rem 1.5rem;\n    border-radius: 4px;\n    font-weight: 600;\n    margin-top: 1rem;\n    transition: background 0.15s ease;\n  }\n  .cta:hover { background: var(--accent); }\n  code {\n    background: #f0ece2;\n    padding: 0.12em 0.4em;\n    border-radius: 3px;\n    font-size: 0.92em;\n  }\n  footer {\n    margin-top: 3rem;\n    padding-top: 1.5rem;\n    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);\n    font-size: 0.85rem;\n    color: var(--muted);\n  }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div class=\"wrap\">\n  <header>\n    <div class=\"eyebrow\">Saturday workshop</div>\n    <h1>Intro to Git</h1>\n    <p class=\"lede\">A hands-on morning for people who have heard \"just commit it\" one too many times.</p>\n  </header>\n\n  <dl class=\"meta\">\n    <dt>When</dt><dd>Saturday — 10:00 AM to 1:00 PM</dd>\n    <dt>Where</dt><dd>TBD (link sent after RSVP)</dd>\n    <dt>Bring</dt><dd>A laptop with Git installed</dd>\n    <dt>Cost</dt><dd>Free</dd>\n  </dl>\n\n  <a class=\"cta\" href=\"#rsvp\">RSVP</a>\n\n  <h2>Who it's for</h2>\n  <p>Anyone who writes code (or writing, or config, or anything text-shaped) and wants to stop being afraid of the command line. No prior Git experience assumed — we start from <code>git init</code>.</p>\n\n  <h2>What you'll leave with</h2>\n  <ul>\n    <li>A working mental model of commits, branches, and remotes</li>\n    <li>Confidence to <code>clone</code>, <code>commit</code>, <code>push</code>, and <code>pull</code></li>\n    <li>The three commands that get you unstuck when things go sideways</li>\n    <li>A real repo on GitHub, made by you, during the session</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h2>Rough agenda</h2>\n  <ul>\n    <li><strong>10:00</strong> — What Git actually is (and isn't)</li>\n    <li><strong>10:30</strong> — Your first repo, commit by commit</li>\n    <li><strong>11:15</strong> — Branches, merges, and the undo button</li>\n    <li><strong>12:00</strong> — GitHub: pushing, pulling, pull requests</li>\n    <li><strong>12:45</strong> — Open Q&amp;A</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h2 id=\"rsvp\">RSVP</h2>\n  <p>Seats are limited so we can keep it hands-on. Email <a href=\"mailto:bear@bearbrown.co\">bear@bearbrown.co</a> with your name and one thing you'd like to be able to do with Git by lunchtime.</p>\n\n  <footer>\n    Hosted by Bear. Coffee provided. Questions welcome.\n  </footer>\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
